      "description": "Watch Namibia vs Congo highlights and goals from Africa Cup of Nations on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 24, 2026. The Africa Cup of Nations group stage intensified on September 24, 2026 , as Namibia and Congo locked horns in a pivotal encounter. Both nations entered the pitch with high ambitions, looking to establish their dominance in one of football's most prestigious tournaments. A Cagey Opening Half The first half was a tactical chess match, with both Namibia and Congo prioritizing defensive solidity over all-out attack. While there were flashes of brilliance and half-chances for both sides, neither could find the decisive touch to break the deadlock before the interval, leaving the match finely balanced. Muzeu Finds the Breakthrough The momentum shifted immediately after the restart. In the 47th minute, B. Muzeu capitalized on a key opportunity to fire Namibia into a 1-0 lead. The goal breathed new life into the contest, forcing Congo to abandon their conservative approach and push forward in search of an equalizer. Defensive Resilience and Late Tension As the second half progressed, the physical nature of the game increased. P. I. Amutenya received a yellow card in the 76th minute as Namibia fought to protect their slender advantage. Despite a late push from Congo , which saw B. Passi booked in stoppage time at 90+6', the Namibian defense held firm to claim all three points and secure a vital win."
