      "description": "Watch Tunisia vs Uganda highlights and goals from Africa Cup of Nations on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 24, 2026. The Africa Cup of Nations delivered another compelling chapter as Tunisia and Uganda locked horns in a tactical battle for supremacy. On this September 24, 2026 , both nations stepped onto the pitch knowing that every decision and every sprint could define their journey in this prestigious tournament. A Tactical Opening The first half saw Tunisia attempting to dictate the tempo through superior ball circulation, while Uganda remained compact and disciplined. The match was a game of chess in the early stages, with neither side willing to overextend and leave gaps at the back. Despite the tactical pressure, clear-cut scoring chances were hard to come by as both defenses stood tall under the warm afternoon sun. Mato Strikes Back The momentum shifted significantly in the second half . After Tunisia took the lead, the onus was on Uganda to find a way back into the contest. Their persistence paid off in the 68th minute when R. Mato found space in the final third and clinicaly converted to level the score at 1-1. The goal revitalized the Ugandan side, turning the final twenty minutes into a frantic search for a decisive winner by both nations. Late Drama and Discipline As the game entered stoppage time, the physical nature of the contest intensified. The referee was forced to intervene in the 90+2 minute, issuing yellow cards to S. Kadida of Tunisia and A. A. Kayondo of Uganda as tempers flared. Despite the late pressure from the Tunisian attack, the Ugandan defense held firm to ensure the spoils were shared in a hard-fought encounter."
